# Route reset — the race (route A), throttle held until the car runs off the end of the straight and hits the barrier, then SELECT
# held (a real press: the mod reads the controller, not this script, so the check gives it the button with GT_MOD_RESET_FAKE), then a
# throttle press after the reset, for tools/mod_reset_check.sh.
# Timeline (measured 2026-11-07 with the mod's step log, `--decomp off`): the game runs ~0.48 player-car physics steps per vblank (~2
# vblanks per step; deterministic, not exactly constant), the race starts (GO, the car answers the throttle) at step ~750. The throttle is held to step ~1725 (+3430), the car leaves the asphalt at step ~1850 and
# hits the barrier (x ~ -450); the check's fake button is held from step 1851 (fires at 1880, ~+3753, while the crash's spin is still going); SELECT is held
# +3690..+3770; the throttle goes down again at +3840 (step ~1925) for 185 vblanks (~90 steps: the car reaches ~4 m/s and then coasts uphill), short enough that the restored car (47 m before the
# barrier) stays clear of it. Pages: see chase.pad.
3300:START,
WAIT:seek=0x1fa48900,2300:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1cf2a980,300:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1cdb9140,300:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1d04fc40,300:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1cf2a980,300:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1cd6db80,300:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1d0332c0,300:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1cf2a980,300:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1cd7d200,300:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1d043c80,300:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1cf2a980,300:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1cc98cc0,400:CROSS,
WAIT:seek=0x1d19db00,1500:CROSS:1450,3070:CROSS:360,3690:SELECT:80,3840:CROSS:185
